WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
A bus needs a safe route through the city.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
A digital twin uses road conditions to plan the route.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The route is ready before the bus reaches the junction.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
If the twin has not received the latest road conditions,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
even an on-time instruction can be useless or cause harm.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
What if we update every digital state immediately?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
At scale, those updates compete for limited bandwidth.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Sending everything can leave important changes waiting.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Different state updates have different value for a task.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Age or frequency of change alone cannot tell us that value.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:28.000
We need to prioritize updates that matter to the decision.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Digital twins also run many tasks that require computation.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:44.000
At scale, these tasks are distributed across edge and cloud resources.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Limited resources and tight deadlines make scheduling difficult.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Execution and state updates must be coordinated to meet those deadlines.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Scheduling problems involve diverse objectives and constraints.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:16.000
No single scheduling method works best for every problem.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:24.000
We study these problems through modeling and theoretical optimization.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:32.000
We develop and evaluate methods for execution and state updates.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:40.000
We will explore agentic methods to adapt scheduling as conditions change.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:48.000
We also explore how AI can generate scheduling algorithms.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:56.000
AI-generated algorithm candidates must be checked and evaluated.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:04.000
These approaches support timely and useful digital twin decisions.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Our goal is to build better digital twins that improve everyday life.